# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Environment template. Copy to `.env` and fill in. NEVER commit real values.
#
# ⚠️ NAMING — two schemes work, `VRCL_SUPA_*` wins.
# `VRCL_SUPA_*` is this project's canonical prefix and what the code prefers. A
# Vercel Supabase integration writes UNPREFIXED names instead (`POSTGRES_URL`,
# `SUPABASE_URL`, `SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`, …). The code accepts both — `VRCL_SUPA_*`
# first, unprefixed as a fallback — so a pasted integration export still runs.
# Prefer `VRCL_SUPA_*` when you have the choice.
#
# Historical note: production once had ONLY the unprefixed set, which the app
# did not read at the time, so `getDbPool()` threw and the site rendered an
# empty catalogue. The fallback exists so that can no longer happen silently.
#
# ⚠️ Vercel bakes env into each deployment at BUILD time, so after any change
# here or in the project settings, redeploy and require `GET /api/health` to
# report {"status":"ok","db":"up"} before trusting the site. A DB failure shows
# up in the UI as "0 artworks", not as an error.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Supabase / PostgreSQL — canonical (VRCL_SUPA_*) ──────────────────────────
# Server side (src/server/db.ts). `POSTGRES_PRISMA_URL` is the pooled connection
# used for queries; `..._NON_POOLING` is required by pg_dump / migration scripts.
# Query parameters are stripped before use, so ?sslmode=... is optional here.
VRCL_SUPA_POSTGRES_PRISMA_URL=
VRCL_SUPA_POSTGRES_URL=
VRCL_SUPA_POSTGRES_URL_NON_POOLING=

# Server side (src/server/db.ts) — service-role key. Server only; never expose.
VRCL_SUPA_SUPABASE_URL=
VRCL_SUPA_SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
# ⚠️ Not read by any code path today — the JWT is verified via the anon/service
# keys, not this secret. Kept because it is set in Vercel and removing it is a
# separate decision; do not assume it is required.
VRCL_SUPA_SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET=

# Browser side (src/lib/supabase.ts). Vite inlines anything prefixed
# NEXT_PUBLIC_/VITE_/VRCL_ at build time — treat these as PUBLIC.
NEXT_PUBLIC_VRCL_SUPA_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_VRCL_SUPA_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_VRCL_SUPA_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# There is deliberately no hardcoded fallback host in the code. If these are
# missing, auth is disabled and data endpoints fail — loudly. Do not "fix" that
# by hardcoding a project URL; a stale literal silently points at the wrong
# project, which is exactly how the October 2026 cutover went unnoticed.

# ── Supabase / PostgreSQL — optional unprefixed aliases ──────────────────────
# Written by the Vercel integration and accepted as fallbacks. Leave blank when
# the VRCL_SUPA_* block above is filled; set them only when pasting a raw
# integration export. `VRCL_SUPA_*` wins wherever both are present.
# POSTGRES_PRISMA_URL=
# POSTGRES_URL=
# POSTGRES_URL_NON_POOLING=
# POSTGRES_HOST=
# POSTGRES_USER=
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
# POSTGRES_DATABASE=
# SUPABASE_URL=
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=
# SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# ── Cloudinary — RESERVED, deliberately retained ─────────────────────────────
# The catalogue moved to Supabase Storage in v3.1/v3.2, so NO code reads these
# credentials any more. The account is still active and is being kept for a
# different future purpose — do not delete these or cancel the account.
# (One hardcoded res.cloudinary.com URL survives as an unused image fallback in
# src/components/AboutView.tsx; the registry resolves that photo from Supabase,
# so nothing is actually served from Cloudinary today.)
CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=
CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=
CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=
# Single-URL form of the three values above.
CLOUDINARY_URL=

# ── Resend (email) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
RESEND_API_KEY=
RESEND_EMAIL_DOMAIN=
# Verifies the signature on POST /api/email/webhook. If unset, webhooks are rejected.
RESEND_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ── Outbound mail routing — server/lib/emailRouting.ts ──────────────────────
#   live     = deliver to the real recipients (production only)
#   redirect = replace recipients with EMAIL_REDIRECT_TO and prefix "[PREVIEW]"
#   off      = send nothing
# Unset => inferred from VERCEL_ENV (production->live, preview->redirect, local->live).
EMAIL_MODE=
# Required whenever EMAIL_MODE=redirect; if missing, mail is SUPPRESSED rather
# than sent to the real recipient.
EMAIL_REDIRECT_TO=
# Studio notification recipients: primary address, plus comma-separated copies.
# ADMIN_EMAIL defaults to rory@ventureio.com; STUDIO_CC defaults to
# jaden@venturepilot.org. Set STUDIO_CC= (empty) to stop copying the second address.
ADMIN_EMAIL=
STUDIO_CC=

# ── Scheduled off-site backup (Vercel Cron -> /api/cron/backup -> Vercel Blob) ──
# Presented by Vercel Cron as "Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET". If unset the
# endpoint refuses every request (it fails closed).
CRON_SECRET=
# Blob store read/write token. Created by linking a Blob store to the project;
# on Vercel the platform token is used, so this is mainly needed locally.
# NEVER commit the value.
BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=

# ── Branded email (optional — sensible defaults are built in) ───────────────
# Public origin for links in emails. Falls back through PUBLIC_SITE_URL and
# VITE_SITE_URL, then to https://roryskagenart.com.
SITE_URL=
# Absolute URL for the brand mark; falls back to ${SITE_URL}/android-chrome-192x192.png
BRAND_LOGO_URL=

# ── Intentionally NOT part of this template ─────────────────────────────────
# GITHUB_TOKEN            — not read by the app, and the value previously kept
#                           here was not a usable credential. Use `gh` instead.
# VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN       — injected by the platform at runtime; never set by hand.
# BLOB_STORE_ID           — not read by any code path.
